{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Follow-up to the MCP cross-session warning story (734d). That story covers all single-ticket mutation tools plus `show_ticket`, including `transition_ticket`/`reopen_ticket` via an additive dict key. Three single-ticket tools remain deferred because their current return contracts do not yet carry the warning: `check_ac` and `quality_check` return `GateResultOut`, and `declare_no_file_impact` currently returns a bare string acknowledgement. Extend the cross-session warning to these three so the MCP structured-response surface matches the CLI warning behavior.\n\n## Approach\n\n- Add optional `cross_session_warning: str | None = None` to the shared `GateResultOut` model so `check_ac` and `quality_check` can carry the same advisory field without changing their existing gate fields.\n- In `_mcp_reads.check_ac` and `_mcp_reads.quality_check`, compute the existing `_cross_session(ticket_id)` warning and attach it to the model returned from `rebar.check_ac` / `rebar.quality_check`.\n- Change `_mcp_writes.declare_no_file_impact` from a bare string ack to the existing `WriteAckOut` / `_ack()` additive ack shape so it can include `result: \"ok\"` plus optional `cross_session_warning`.\n- Remove the `structured_output=False` registration override from the `declare_no_file_impact` MCP tool; once the tool returns an object with a schema, it must participate in the normal structured output contract instead of advertising an unstructured string response.\n- Update the no-schema/schema expectations for `declare_no_file_impact`: tests that previously expected no output schema or a bare string acknowledgement must now expect the existing write-ack object schema with `result` constrained to the value `\"ok\"` and optional `cross_session_warning`.\n- Update the MCP cross-session tests and output-schema expectations so the structured response contract is explicit.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Extend `tests/unit/test_cross_session_mcp.py` so a ticket held by another session returns `cross_session_warning` from MCP `check_ac`, `quality_check`, and `declare_no_file_impact`; the test should fail before implementation because the first two lack the field and the third returns a string.\n- Extend the same test module's schema assertion so `GateResultOut` advertises optional `cross_session_warning`.\n- Update schema/coverage tests that intentionally encoded `declare_no_file_impact` as an unstructured string ack, including the no-schema/schema expectations.\n- Run targeted tests: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_cross_session_mcp.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_output_schema_coverage.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_file_impact_scope_heldout.py`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] MCP `check_ac` returns the existing gate verdict fields plus optional `cross_session_warning`, checked by a unit test that exercises a cross-session claim.\n- [ ] MCP `quality_check` returns the existing gate verdict fields plus optional `cross_session_warning`, checked by a unit test that exercises a cross-session claim.\n- [ ] MCP `declare_no_file_impact` returns the existing additive `WriteAckOut` ack object containing `result: \"ok\"` and optional `cross_session_warning`, checked by a unit test that exercises a cross-session claim.\n- [ ] The `declare_no_file_impact` MCP registration no longer uses `structured_output=False`, and the MCP output schemas/schema coverage tests reflect the existing `WriteAckOut` fields (`result: \"ok\"`, optional warning fields) rather than the old no-schema/string expectation.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788770513056284001,"uuid":"d3915b9e-96d6-4f00-a78f-410c12283614"}